# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# Each projected callable owns S and S's full source. The local name y must
# not be substituted with the outer model's bound y while S is constructed.
# Reusing w after constructing u checks the same outer binding is retained;
# descriptor independence requires a separate physical-identity observer.
fn: add (int: y; int: x) int
    S:
        int: y 2
        y: y + 1
    S
    return: y + x + S\y
fn: wrap (int: k) fn: (int: x) int
    return: merge(y: k; add)
@: w wrap(5)
@: u wrap(100)
int: a (w: 1)
int: b (u: 1)
int: c (w: 1)
int: ok 0
if: a = 9 && b = 104 && c = 9
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
